# --- apps/ ignores: read this before adding a rule (revised 2026-07-16) ---
# Built apps are USER DATA. They must stay tracked, because the version
# timeline and rollback read `git log -- apps/<slug>/`
# (routes_projects.list_app_versions_core). Only OUR OWN test junk belongs here.
#
# NEVER add an `apps/<verb>-*/` rule. _slugify (routes_aiuibuilder.py:187)
# builds a slug from the first five words of the user's build description, so
# such a rule eats real user apps by construction and does it silently, since
# `git add` on an ignored path is a no-op. The rules removed here
# (create-me-*, make-the-*, me-a-*, upload-*, *smoke*) were swallowing 11 real
# apps on prod, 8 via create-me-* alone.
#
# Generated test apps belong under the `_test-` prefix: _slugify collapses
# non-alphanumeric runs and drops leading empties, so a user description can
# never reach that namespace. Covered by tests/test_gitignore_app_slugs.py.
apps/_test-*/
apps/alama-flight/
apps/browser-smoke-*/
apps/build-smoke-*/
apps/caddy-auth-test-*/
apps/crudsimple/
apps/diag-test/
apps/e2e-4f3e4b/
apps/foo-app/
apps/landing-page-for-aiui-bot-*/
apps/ralph-portfolio/
apps/smoke-upload-*/
apps/test-crud/
apps/test-project/
apps/testfly/
apps/upload-c2f78c78/
apps/upload-da5312a9/
